1) I think doors are a generally good thing, and the different
characters for open and closed doors will solve any problems I have
with it.  Hitting 'o' doesn't bother me, from playing Moria, which
brings us to...

2) Did someone say that there should be gems lodged within the walls
of the dungeon?  I think this would be an unneccesary addition.  Not
that it would bother me either.

3) Someone else said something about water.  I hope the intention was
not to have drinking water be as essential as eating food.  While this
would not neccesarily require more water potions, (fountains and sinks
should contain water.  Potions should contain enchanted water.) it
would just be a pain.  We can add as many features as we want to
promote realism, but if it adds nothing too new to the game, and
doesn't fix some glaring inconsistency in the game (like the picking
up food you can't carry when eating it bug), I'm against it.  We could
give players callouses on their feet if they walk too much.  We could
make hair grow, and if you don't find a pair of scissors, it
interferes with your fighting.  We could make fingernails grow, which
you would have to eat every 300 turns to keep them trim.  We could
make players and monsters defecate, leaving a trail of
  f - 3 piles of dog feces
around.  What would be the point.

Of course, I have a sneaking suspicion I completely misinterpreted
that article, because I don't seem to have it around anymore...

